//# Notations on the hardcopy document read, in part:
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:26
//#
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:27
//#	Assemble revision 001 of AGC program LMY99 by NASA 2021112-061
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:28
//#	16:27 JULY 14, 1969
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:29
//
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:30
//# Page 90
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:31
//# CONVENTIONS AND NOTATIONS UTILIZED FOR ERASABLE ASSIGNMENTS.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:32
//
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:33
//#	EQUALS	IS USED IN TWO WAYS.  IT IS OFTEN USED TO CHAIN A GROUP
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:34
//#		OF ASSIGNMENTS SO THAT THE GROUP MAY BE MOVED WITH THE
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:35
//#		CHANGING OF ONLY ONE CARD.  EXAMPLE:
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:36
//#
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:37
//#			X	EQUALS	START
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:38
//#			Y	EQUALS	X	+SIZE.X
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:39
//#			Z	EQUALS	Y	+SIZE.Y
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:40
//#
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:41
//#		(X, Y, AND Z ARE CONSECUTIVE AND BEGIN AT START.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:42
//#		SIZE.X AND SIZE.Y ARE THE RESPECTIVE SIZES OF X AND Y.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:43
//#		USUALLY NUMERIC, IE. 1, 2, 6, 18D, ETC.)
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:44
//
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:45
//#	EQUALS	OFTEN IMPLIES THE SHARING OF REGISTERS (DIFFERENT NAMES
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:46
//#		AND DIFFERENT DATA).  EXAMPLE:
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:47
//#
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:48
//#			X	EQUALS	Y
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:49
//
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:50
//#	=	MEANS THAT MULTIPLE NAMES HAVE BEEN GIVEN TO THE SAME DATA.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:51
//#		(THIS IS LOGICAL EQUIVALENCE, NOT SHARING.)  EXAMPLE:
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:52
//#
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:53
//#			X	=	Y
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:54
//
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:55
//#	THE SIZE AND UTILIZATION OF AN ERASABLE ARE OFTEN INCLUDED IN
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:56
//#	THE COMMENTS IN THE FOLLOWING FORM:  M(SIZE)N.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:57
//#
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:58
//#		M	REFERS TO THE MOBILITY OF THE ASSIGNMENT.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:59
//#			B	MEANS THAT THE SYMBOL IS REFERENCED BY BASIC
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:60
//#				INSTRUCTIONS AND THUS IS E-BANK SENSITIVE.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:61
//#			I	MEANS THAT THE SYMBOL IS REFERENCED ONLY BY
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:62
//#				INTERPRETIVE INSTRUCTIONS, AND IS THUS E-BANK
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:63
//#				INSENSITIVE AND MAY APPEAR IN ANY E-BANK.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:64
//#
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:65
//#		SIZE	IS THE NUMBER OF REGISTERS INCLUDED BY THE SYMBOL.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:66
//#
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:67
//#		N	INDICATES THE NATURE OF PERMANENCE OF THE CONTENTS.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:68
//#			PL	MEANS THAT THE CONTENTS ARE PAD LOADED.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:69
//#			DSP	MEANS THAT THE REGISTER IS USED FOR A DISPLAY.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:70
//#			PRM	MEANS THAT THE REGISTER IS PERMANENT.  IE., IT
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:71
//#				IS USED DURING THE ENTIRE MISSION FOR ONE
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:72
//#				PURPOSE AND CANNOT BE SHARED.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:73
//#			TMP	MEANS THAT THE REGISTER IS USED TEMPORARILY OR
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:74
//#				IS A SCRATCH REGISTER FOR THE ROUTINE TO WHICH
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:75
//#				IT IS ASSIGNED.  THAT IS, IT NEED NOT BE SET
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:76
//#				PRIOR TO INVOCATION OF THE ROUTINE NOR DOES IT
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:77
//#				CONTAIN USEFUL OUTPUT TO ANOTHER ROUTINE.  THUS
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:78
//# Page 91
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:79
//#				IT MAY BE SHARED WITHANY OTHER ROUTINE WHICH
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:80
//#				IS NOT ACTIVE IN PARALLEL
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:81
//#			IN	MEANS INPUT TO THE ROUTINE AND IT IS PROBABLY
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:82
//#				TEMPORARY FOR A HIGHER-LEVEL ROUTINE/PROGRAM.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:83
//#			OUT	MEANS OUTPUT FROM THE ROUTINE, PROBABLY
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:84
//#				TEMPORARY FOR A HIGHER-LEVEL ROUTINE/PROGRAM.
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:85
//
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:86
//# Page 92
// PORT: SOURCE ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:87
